{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-17T21:58:37.940Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"ddb2e572b3dc24915ab9fe76","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","lineage:pm-03q389","lineage:pm-i7w2"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-03q389","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","lineage:pm-03q389","lineage:pm-i7w2"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.326","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1749"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1749: adding a secret-guard rule breaks typed consumers' exhaustive Record<SecretGuardFinding['rule'], ...> policy maps; offer a stable category per rule and a default-plus-overrides policy helper"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub issue 1749 (fleet report): extensions that type a per-rule secret guard policy as an exhaustive Record over SecretGuardFinding['rule'] failed tsc with TS2741 on the 2026.11.13 bump, when the rule union gained credential_key_assignment. The detector was additive, but for exhaustive typed consumers it is a breaking type change that the release notes did not flag. Proposed: export a stable category per rule (for example credential, identity, path, network) and a policy helper such as a default decision plus partial overrides with a decide function, so a new credential rule inherits refuse without breaking compilation; and list new rule literals under a typed-consumers note in release notes. Related: the secret-guard family pm-hw00c2 (credential-key reference literals) and pm-x07qz2 (property names) changed the same finding type."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["api-design","gh:1749","sdk","secret-guard","typed-consumers"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-17T21:58:37.940Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-17T21:58:37.940Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The SDK exports a stable per-rule category map and a policy helper that decides a finding from a default plus partial overrides, typed so adding a rule never breaks a consumer that uses it; the SDK surface snapshot records the addition; release notes or the SDK migration notes call out new rule literals for exhaustive consumers; tests prove a newly added rule inherits the category default"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-doxj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Adding a detector does not break typed consumers on a calendar bump, or the SDK offers a supported default-plus-overrides policy"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"An exhaustive Record over the rule union fails TS2741 whenever a rule is added"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"sdk"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-hw00c2","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-17T21:58:37.940Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-x07qz2","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-17T21:58:37.940Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b148