{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T10:52:32.013Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-43p2c3","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-43p2c3+pm-5kfzjh+pm-gh1749","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-43p2c3","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-18T10:52:32.013Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"PR 1752 bot review, first pass: CodeRabbit on fd842f55f and Greptile. The policy findings and how each was fixed:\n- Greptile P2: with default typed as Exclude<Decision, undefined>, TypeScript could not infer Decision from the default, so an unannotated decideSecretGuardFinding({ default: true }, finding) returned unknown. Fix: default is Decision & ({} | null), which infers from the default. It still rejects undefined, including for SecretGuardPolicy<unknown> (CodeRabbit), and still allows null. Type tests cover the inferred boolean and string defaults, the unknown undefined default and a null default.\n- CodeRabbit: decideSecretGuardFinding read finding.rule and policy.default twice, so a getter could pass validation and then return something else. Fix: each is read once into a local. A getter test asserts a single read.\n- CodeRabbit: the future-detector test reused the statically imported guard when run alone with -t. Fix: vi.resetModules() before vi.doMock. It passes when run alone.\n- CodeRabbit: the runtime-entrypoint test claim was already fixed in c564fc892."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T10:52:32.013Z"}],"before_hash":"ee8a6fb390d16a67ff3ee305b1dd746a6c01bf8b1889201a96ba431bda077ce6","after_hash":"498089134517f7a4d8326935f4993d15d5abc77ce31671a7ce272458a86f54d4","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4e1b092506f9718c06256485575406dd7f47e2d43b883edb5232ec1cd5d5d87c"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T11:25:36.337Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"release-operator","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","release:pm-9x9drr"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-43p2c3+pm-5kfzjh+pm-gh1749","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","release:pm-9x9drr"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-18T11:25:36.337Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 4 (gpt-6.2-sol, xhigh, on 67c7eef6b). The policy findings and how each was handled:\n- P1: the default type Decision & ({} | null) failed @typescript-eslint/no-empty-object-type in the static gate. My eslint run had not covered mutation-guard.ts after that change. Fix: NonNullable<Decision> | Extract<Decision, null>. A tsc probe and the type tests confirm the same behaviour: default-only policies infer their decision type, undefined is rejected (including for SecretGuardPolicy<unknown>), and null stays a valid decision.\n- P3, declined with reason: a rules object assigned through a variable can carry extra keys whose values fail the Decision type. That is TypeScript's general structural-typing gap for non-fresh objects. Fresh literals still get excess-property checks, which catch typos (pinned by a type test), and an index signature would give up that typo check. At runtime only an exact own key decides."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T11:25:36.337Z"}],"before_hash":"498089134517f7a4d8326935f4993d15d5abc77ce31671a7ce272458a86f54d4","after_hash":"9e73a3924866e497beaa21140fcd449b15184fd25c39196935f6bb727e18f897","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ae0d8b5bfeddf27f8491901e878069a009d1dfd3b754803099c8d0d51746a5b2"}
