{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T11:25:57.073Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"release-operator","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","release:pm-9x9drr"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-43p2c3+pm-5kfzjh+pm-gh1749","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","release:pm-9x9drr"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"close","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"A category-only SecretGuardPolicy compiles whatever the rule union holds (type tests); a mocked future detector inherits its category decision (unit test); unknown, prototype and inherited keys fall back to the default; the release notes list the change under Changed (SDK contract) through its contract_change"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Adding a detector does not break typed consumers, and the SDK offers a supported default-plus-overrides policy"},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/claim_principal"},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/assignee"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T11:25:57.073Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/status","value":"closed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/closed_at","value":"2026-11-18T11:25:57.049Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/completed_at","value":"2026-11-18T11:25:57.049Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/resolution","value":"Every SecretRule declares a required credential, network or path category. The SDK root and governance entrypoints export SecretGuardRule, the literal SecretGuardRuleCategory union, SECRET_GUARD_RULE_CATEGORIES, secretGuardRuleCategory and SecretGuardPolicy plus decideSecretGuardFinding (rule, then category, then default; own properties only; undefined counts as absent; malformed input throws TypeError; the decision type is inferred from the default). A compile-time check ties the SDK union to the rule inventory, and the surface snapshot records the literals. docs/MUTATION_INTEGRITY.md documents category policies, and docs/RELEASING.md documents contract_change declarations, including that a new detector is one."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/close_reason","value":"Secret-guard findings have a stable category per rule and a default-plus-overrides policy helper, so adding a detector never breaks typed consumers"}],"before_hash":"fc26a481622b48a45360505c2da7a6bf4176691c275ab1e71c7bce8bff5e626f","after_hash":"8ea7e80dfeedf58df5232c8a0b84d5e83889ed44c216d3edb377559f59b870ce","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"completion":{"timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:25:57.049Z","source":"close_time"},"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f331bb02eb3e6e0a49286aaf6a81aa53914e0021d3f07a46b4e56d06b9b3bef8"}
